@h1 Install h1@

Wit runs on Node. You need @strong Node 20 or newer strong@.

@h2 The command-line tool h2@

Install the CLI globally:

@@@pre
npm install -g @witlang/cli
pre@@@

Check it works:

@@@pre
wit --version
pre@@@

@h2 As project packages h2@

If you're building on Wit — parsing it, rendering it, embedding it — add the
packages to your project instead:

@@@pre
npm install @witlang/parser @witlang/runtime @witlang/render-html
pre@@@

@h2 What the CLI gives you h2@

@ul
@li @code wit build code@ — compile a document to HTML, Markdown, or PDF li@
@li @code wit fmt code@ — tidy a Wit file's indentation li@
@li @code wit check code@ — report parse and reference errors li@
ul@

Next: write @a |href ../first-document/| your first document a@.
